meta {
  name: Get advocate thread with messages
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/advocate/threads/{{threadId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # GET /api/advocate/threads/{id}

  One thread with its messages, oldest first. Only the parent who started the thread can read it.

  ## Responses

  - `200` — `data: AdvocateThreadDetailDto`
  - `401` — missing/invalid bearer token
  - `404` — thread not found or not owned by the caller

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": null,
    "data": {
      "id": 3,
      "childProfileId": 1,
      "title": "Reading goal progress",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-10T14:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-10T14:05:31Z",
      "lastMessageAt": "2026-09-10T14:05:31Z",
      "messages": [
        {
          "id": 40,
          "role": "User",
          "contentMarkdown": "Is my son on track for his reading goal?",
          "citations": [],
          "suggestions": [],
          "truncated": false,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-10T14:05:00Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "role": "Assistant",
          "contentMarkdown": "Based on the latest progress report ...",
          "citations": [
            { "kind": "goal", "id": 340, "label": "Reading fluency", "parent": { "kind": "iep", "id": 12 } },
            { "kind": "kb", "id": 5, "label": "Measuring goal progress", "parent": null }
          ],
          "suggestions": [
            { "kind": "prep_question", "text": "How is fluency being measured each week?", "id": null, "date": null },
            { "kind": "open_goal", "text": null, "id": 340, "date": null }
          ],
          "truncated": false,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-10T14:05:31Z"
        }
      ],
      "disclaimer": "The Virtual Advocate gives general information ... It is not legal advice. ..."
    },
    "errors": []
  }
  ```

  - `role`: `User | Assistant`
  - `citations[].kind`: `kb | child | iep | etr | progress_report | authored_version | shared_draft | iep_analysis | etr_analysis | progress_report_analysis | analysis_run | iep_section | etr_section | goal | goal_record | comparison | journal | contribution | advocacy_goal | meeting_prep | prep_question | meeting`
  - `citations[].parent`: the record to open the citation inside (goal / iep_section / iep_analysis → iep; etr_section / etr_analysis → etr; progress_report → iep; progress_report_analysis → progress_report), otherwise `null`
  - `suggestions[].kind`: `prep_question | journal_entry | open_kb | open_goal`; `date` (`yyyy-MM-dd`) is set for `journal_entry` only
}
